=== ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS ===
  • Data seam: own protocol `SavingsSlideSource` + `InMemorySavingsSlideSource` (NO `import Shared`) so the
    surface host-compiles WITHOUT the unstaged KMP xcframework. The web `SavingsSlide` is presentational (prop
    `data: YearReview`); the native surface elevates that prop into the P1/S8 cache-then-network state holder
    (the year-review feed) and the view performs ZERO HTTP. A `SavingsSlideModel(data:loading:)` web-prop
    initializer preserves the exact `<SavingsSlide data={data} />` call site.
  • Load state: self-contained `SavingsSlideLoadState` + `SavingsSlideError` mirroring the facade `LoadableState`/
    `FacadeError` SHAPE (cached-behind-refresh, ADR-013 stale, offline-keeps-cache, retryable) — so the production
    binding is a 1:1 map and every branch is unit-testable. The web slide only renders content; the resolver is a
    documented SUPERSET adding the prompt's loading/empty/stale/offline/error chrome around that same composition.
  • Render math parity: `gasCostEquiv = gas_savings + total_charging_cost`; the hero is GROUPED
    (`fmtNumber(value,0)` → "$1,850"), the bar labels are UN-grouped (`$Math.round(...)` → "$2262"), and the
    electric bar width is the integer percentage `round(tcc/equiv*100)` (guarded to 0 when equiv≤0) — verified by
    a dedicated grouping-distinction + zero-guard unit test.
  • Count-up hero: an `@MainActor Animatable` numeric Text (the Swift-6-suggested isolated conformance) reproduces
    the web `AnimatedNumber` ease-out count from 0; jumps straight to target under Reduce Motion (the emoji's
    spring + the bars' fade-in honor Reduce Motion the same way via the shared Motion primitives).
  • i18n: per-surface `.strings` table + `SavingsSlideStrings` facade (NSLocalizedString tableName + value
    fallback) — parallel-safe across the concurrent slots; the shared Localizable.xcstrings is NOT edited
    (Honesty rule 7). The cups note interpolates through a localized `%d` so translators own word order.
  • Telemetry: REUSES the canonical `DashboardWidgetTelemetryEvent` / `DashboardWidgetTelemetrySink` /
    `BufferedDashboardWidgetTelemetry` (Sources/DashboardWidgets/BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift) — the app-wide
    P1/S11 diagnostics seam. `SavingsSlide.viewOpenedEvent == .viewOpened(surface:"SavingsSlide")`, emitted on `.task`.
  • Units note: the slide renders CURRENCY (`gas_savings`, `total_charging_cost`), not unit-suffixed physical
    quantities — no Mi/Mph/Kwh fields are touched, so the Phase-48 SI-canonical rules do not apply to this surface.

